{
 "title": "Slide Settings: Fit, Trim, Loop and Volume — LayerCue from Zero, Episode 7",
 "version": 1,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "chapter": "Two places",
   "start": 0,
   "end": 0,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "Welcome back! Today, we fix a slide before it goes out.",
     "pause": 0,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "Two places change how a slide plays.",
     "pause": 0,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "The control row on the left changes only what's playing right now. It isn't saved.",
     "pause": 0.6,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "Slide settings, on the right, is saved with that one slide.",
     "pause": 0,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "To load a slide there, click its name, or Option-click it. Nothing goes out.",
     "pause": 2.4,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "chapter": "Scale",
   "start": 0,
   "end": 0,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "A new slide starts on Fit. It shows the whole picture, but can leave black bars.",
     "pause": 1.4,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "Fill fills the screen, and cuts off what spills over.",
     "pause": 1.2,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "Stretch ignores the proportions.",
     "pause": 1.2,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "Fit plus blur fills the empty sides with a blurred copy. That's the one for a vertical phone video.",
     "pause": 1.4,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "chapter": "Crop and fit",
   "start": 0,
   "end": 0,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "The gear on the preview opens Crop and fit.",
     "pause": 1.6,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "Drag the handles to choose the part you want to keep.",
     "pause": 2.6,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "The Result shows what the audience will see.",
     "pause": 1.0,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "Every change is saved at once. Done just closes the sheet.",
     "pause": 1.2,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "chapter": "In and out points",
   "start": 0,
   "end": 0,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "This video starts with two seconds of black, and ends with credits.",
     "pause": 0,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "Move the bar to where it should start, and press In point.",
     "pause": 2.4,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "Move it to where it should end, and press Out point.",
     "pause": 2.4,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "Now a click on the card plays only the part in between.",
     "pause": 2.6,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s5",
   "chapter": "Speed and repeat",
   "start": 0,
   "end": 0,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "The speed chip here is saved with the slide.",
     "pause": 1.6,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "The one in the control row looks the same, but it isn't saved.",
     "pause": 0,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "The repeat button chooses Loop or Play once.",
     "pause": 2.4,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s6",
   "chapter": "Slide volume",
   "start": 0,
   "end": 0,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "The purple bar is the slide's own volume, and it's saved.",
     "pause": 1.6,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "When the slide goes out, its layer starts at that level.",
     "pause": 2.0,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "On the background, a slide starts silent. That's on purpose.",
     "pause": 2.4,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s7",
   "chapter": "To Screen",
   "start": 0,
   "end": 0,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "To Screen puts the slide on stage without playing it.",
     "pause": 1.6,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "It holds on the frame where the bar stands.",
     "pause": 0.8,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "Then start it on cue, with play in the control row.",
     "pause": 2.6,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "s9",
   "chapter": "What's next",
   "start": 0,
   "end": 0,
   "lines": [
    {
     "text": "You can now fix a slide before it goes out.",
     "pause": 0,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    },
    {
     "text": "Next time: presentation settings, for fades and timing.",
     "pause": 0,
     "screen": "",
     "action": "",
     "caption": "",
     "keys": ""
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}